hadiths[39]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1296","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when we used to eat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we would not put our hands (in the food) until he started and put his hand (first). Once, we were present with him at a meal when a girl came running as if someone was driving her, and she tried to put her hand in the food, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) caught her hand. Then a Bedouin came running, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) caught his hand as well. Then he said: ""The Shaytan gains power over food on which the name of Allah is not mentioned, and he brought this girl to gain power over this food, so I caught her hand. Then he brought this Bedouin for the same purpose, so I caught his hand too. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, Shaytan's hand is with their hands in my hand."" And in another narration, it is mentioned that then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said ""Bismillah"" and began to eat."
"1297","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a person enters his house, and at the time of entering and eating food he mentions the name of Allah, then Satan (says to his companions and followers): ""There is neither a place for you to stay here, nor food."" But when he does not mention the name of Allah upon entering the house, Satan says: ""You have found a place to stay."" And when he does not mention the name of Allah at the time of eating as well, Satan says: ""You have found both a place to stay and food."
"1298","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for indeed Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."
"1299","Sayyiduna Iyas bin Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: A man ate with his left hand in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Eat with your right hand.” He replied, “I cannot.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “May you not be able to.” He had said this out of arrogance. The narrator says that he was never able to raise that hand to his mouth for the rest of his life."
"1300","Sayyiduna Umar bin Abi Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was in the lap of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (because the Prophet (peace be upon him) had married Umar's mother, Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her)), and my hand was moving all around in the bowl. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O boy, mention the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near to you."
"1301","Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat with three fingers and would lick them before wiping his hand."
"1302","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When any of you eats food, he should not wipe his hand until he has licked it himself or has had it licked by someone else."
"1303","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that the fingers and the vessel be licked (cleaned), and said: ""You do not know in which morsel or part of the food the blessing is."
"1304","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""Satan is present with each one of you at every action he does, even when he is eating. If any of you drops a morsel, he should clean off any dirt and eat it, and not leave it for Satan. When he finishes eating, he should lick his fingers, for he does not know in which part of the food the blessing lies."
"1305","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty is pleased with His servant when he eats and says (Alhamdulillah) or drinks and says (Alhamdulillah) (i.e., after eating at morning, evening, or any other time)."
"1306","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) once went out during the night or day and saw Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both). He asked, ""What has brought you out of your homes at this hour?"" They replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! Hunger has driven us out."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I too have come out for the same reason. Come."" Then they went along with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the door of an Ansari man, but he was not at home. His wife saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and welcomed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Where is so-and-so (referring to her husband)?"" She replied, ""He has gone to fetch sweet water for us."" (From this hadith, it is understood that it is permissible to speak to a non-mahram woman out of necessity and to reply to her, and likewise, a woman may invite a man into the house whose coming would please her husband.) Meanwhile, the Ansari man arrived and, seeing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his two companions, said, ""Praise be to Allah! No one has such guests today as I have."" Then he went and brought a bunch of dates containing unripe, dry, and fresh dates, and said, ""Eat from this."" Then he took a knife, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do not slaughter a goat that gives milk."" So he slaughtered another goat, and they all ate its meat, ate dates, and drank water. When they were satisfied, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, on the Day of Resurrection you will be questioned about this blessing: you left your homes due to hunger, and did not return until you received this blessing."
"1307","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a neighbor who used to make excellent broth; he was Persian. Once, he made broth for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and came to invite him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Is Aisha also invited?"" He replied, ""No."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Then I will not come."" He came again to invite him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Is Aisha also invited?"" He replied, ""No."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Then I will not come."" Then, for the third time, he came to invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Is Aisha also invited?"" He said, ""Yes."" Then both of them (i.e., the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her) went together until they reached his house."
"1308","Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that among the Ansar there was a man named Abu Shu’aib, who had a slave that used to sell meat. This Ansari saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and noticed signs of hunger on his face, so he said to his slave, “Prepare food for five people, for I wish to invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he will be the fifth among them.” The narrator says that he prepared the food. Then he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and invited him, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) was the fifth among the five. Another man joined them, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reached the door, he said (to the host), “This man has come along with us; if you wish, you may permit him, otherwise he will return.” He said, “No, O Messenger of Allah! Rather, I give him permission.”"
"1309","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said that he was in great distress (regarding food and drink). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a message to one of his noble wives, and she replied, ""By the One Who has sent you with the truth, I have nothing except water."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent to another wife, and she replied the same, until all the noble wives (may Allah be pleased with them) gave the same answer: ""We have nothing except water."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Who will host this person tonight? May Allah have mercy on him."" Then an Ansari stood up and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I will do it."" He took the man to his place and said to his wife, ""Do you have anything?"" She replied, ""Nothing, except the food for my children."" The Ansari said, ""Distract the children with something, and when our guest comes in and we begin to eat, extinguish the lamp."" So when they began to eat, she got up and turned off the lamp. (The narrator says) They sat, and the guest ate. They did as planned, and the husband and wife remained hungry while the guest ate the food. In the morning, the Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Allah was amazed (i.e., pleased) at what you did with your guest last night."
"1310","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The food of two persons suffices for three, and the food of three suffices for four."
"1311","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The food of one is sufficient for two, the food of two is sufficient for four, and the food of four is sufficient for eight."
"1312","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir and Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A believer eats in one intestine, and a disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"1313","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a guest came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he was a disbeliever. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) hosted him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that the milk of a goat be milked, and he drank it. Then (the milk of) a second goat was milked, and he drank that too. Then (the milk of) a third goat was milked, and he drank that too, until he drank the milk of seven goats. Then, the next morning, he became a Muslim. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that the milk of a goat be milked, and he drank its milk, then (the milk of) a second goat was milked, but he could not finish it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer drinks in one intestine, and a disbeliever in seven intestines."
"1314","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a person invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I also went with him. Soup was brought in which there was gourd (pumpkin). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started eating the gourd with great relish. When I saw this, I began to put pieces of gourd towards the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not eat them myself. Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that from that day I began to like gourd."
"1315","Talha bin Nafi narrates that he heard from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took my hand and took me to his house. Then a few pieces of bread were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said, ""Is there any condiment?"" They said, ""No, except a little vinegar."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Vinegar is a good condiment."" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""From that day I began to love vinegar, since I heard this from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."" And Talha (who narrates this hadith from Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Since I heard this hadith from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), I also like vinegar."
"1316","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Busr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed with my father, and we presented food and watbah. (Watbah is a dish made by mixing dates, cheese, and ghee.) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ate it. Then dried dates were brought, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would eat them and place the pits between his index and middle fingers and throw them away. Shu’bah said: This is what I think, and I believe this is what is in the hadith, that the pits were placed between the two fingers (meaning, the pits were not mixed with the dates but kept separate). Then something to drink was brought, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) drank and then gave it to the one sitting on his right. Then my father held the reins of the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) animal and requested: Pray for us. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Allah! Bless their sustenance, forgive them, and have mercy on them."
"1317","'Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that' dates were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he began to distribute them, and he was sitting in the manner of one who sits in haste (i.e., squatting), and he was eating from them quickly (perhaps the Prophet, peace be upon him, had some other task to attend to). In another narration, it is mentioned that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the position of Iq‘a’ while eating dates."
"1318","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aisha! The household that does not have dates, its people are hungry."" He said this two or three times."
"1319","Jabala bin Suhaim says that Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) used to give us dates to eat, and in those days people were experiencing hardship (regarding food). We were eating when Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) passed by and said: ""Do not eat two dates together (at once), because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that, except when you have permission from your brother."" Shu’bah said: I think the statement about seeking permission is from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1320","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) eating cucumber with dates."
"1321","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at (the place of) Marr az-Zahran, and we were picking kabath (the fruit of a wild tree), when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pick the black ones. We said: O Messenger of Allah! It seems as if you have grazed goats (since you know about the wilderness)? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! And there has never been a prophet who did not graze goats, or he said something similar."
"1322","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we were going along when at (the place of) Mar al-Zahran we saw a rabbit, so we chased it. The first people ran after it but became tired, then I ran and caught it and brought it to Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him). He slaughtered it and sent its back and both thighs to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I brought them, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) accepted them."
"1323","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Sayyiduna Khalid bin Walid (may Allah be pleased with him), who was called the Sword of Allah, informed that he went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to Umm al-Mu’minin Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), who was the purified wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and the maternal aunt of both Khalid and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). There they found roasted meat of a lizard (dabb), which Maymunah’s sister, Hafidah bint Harith, had brought from Najd. Then she (Maymunah) placed that lizard before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and it was rare that any food was placed before him without it being mentioned and named (as to what it was). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reached his hand towards the lizard, when one of the women present spoke up and said, “Tell the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) what has been placed before him.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah! This is a lizard.” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) withdrew his hand. Sayyiduna Khalid bin Walid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah! Is the lizard forbidden?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “No, it is not forbidden, but it is not found in my land, so I feel a dislike for it.” Sayyiduna Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Then I pulled it towards me and ate it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was watching me eat and did not stop me.”"
"1324","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""We live in a land where there are many lizards, and most of the food of my family is that."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reply to him. We said, ""Ask again."" He asked again, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reply three times. Then, on the third time (or after the third time), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said, ""O Bedouin! Allah, Glorified and Exalted be He, cursed or became angry with a group of the Children of Israel, so He transformed them into animals, and they used to walk on the earth. I do not know whether the lizard is from among those animals or not. Therefore, I do not eat it, nor do I declare it unlawful."
"1325","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we fought seven battles with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and kept eating locusts."
"1326","‘Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent us under the leadership of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him) to meet (i.e., pursue) a caravan of the Quraysh, and for our provisions for the journey, he gave us a bag of dates, and he had nothing else to give us. Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to give us one date each (every day). Abu Az-Zubair said: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), “What would you do with one date?” He said: We would suck it like a child, then drink a little water over it, and that would suffice us for the whole day and night. And we would shake leaves from the trees with our sticks, then soak them in water and eat them. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When we reached the seashore, a long and thick thing appeared there. We went to it and saw that it was an animal called ‘ambergris’ (whale). Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “This is dead (i.e., unlawful).” Then he said: “No, we have been sent by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and we have set out in the way of Allah, and you have been compelled (by hunger), so eat it.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We stayed there for a month, and we were three hundred men. We kept eating its meat until we became fat. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I saw that we would fill pots upon pots with fat from its eye socket, and we would cut pieces of meat from it as big as a bull. Finally, Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) took thirteen of us, and all of them sat inside its eye socket. And from its ribs, he raised one rib and set it upright, then saddled the largest camel we had and it passed underneath it. And we made ‘washa’iq’ from its meat for provisions for the journey (washa’iq are pieces of meat boiled and dried, kept for travel). When we came to Madinah, we went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and related this incident. He said: “That was provision which Allah brought out for you. Do you have any of its meat left? Feed us as well.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We sent some of its meat to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he ate it."
"1327","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that on the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and permitted the eating of horse meat."
"1328","Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) says: We slaughtered a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then we ate its meat."
"1329","Sayyiduna Abu Tha’labah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the meat of those donkeys that live among the people (and the wild donkey, i.e., zebra, is unanimously lawful)."
"1330","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) conquered Khaybar, the donkeys that were coming out from the village, we caught them and cooked their meat. Meanwhile, the announcer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called out: Beware! Allah Almighty and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) both forbid you from (eating) the meat of donkeys, for it is impure and eating it is the work of Satan. Then all the pots were overturned while the meat was boiling in them."
"1331","`Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: It is forbidden to eat the flesh of every predatory animal with fangs."
"1332","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade (the eating of) every predatory animal with fangs and every bird with talons (that eats with its claws)."
"1333","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in the lower part of the house and Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) was in the upper part. Once, Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) woke up at night and said, ""We walk above the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him),"" so he moved and spent the night in a corner. After that, Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to go upstairs, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""The lower part is more comfortable (for those who stay and for those who come, and that is why the Messenger of Allah stayed in the lower part)."" Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I cannot stay on a roof under which you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are."" Upon hearing this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the upper part and Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) came down to the lower part. Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) used to prepare food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the food was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (and he would eat from it and the leftover food would be returned), Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) would ask (the servant), ""Where did the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch the food?"" and he would eat from that place (for blessings). One day, Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) prepared food in which there was garlic. When the food was returned, Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""Where did the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch?"" He was told that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not eat the food. Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) became worried and went upstairs and asked, ""Is garlic forbidden?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""No, but I dislike it."" Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Whatever you dislike, I also dislike."" Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) said that angels used to come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (and the angels are troubled by the smell of garlic, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not eat it)."
"1334","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finding fault with any food. If he desired it, he would eat it, and if he did not desire it, he would remain silent."
